<!--
  Arabic overrides for the Uqudo SDK's own full-screen UI (R-002 / BL-071). S8-09.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, and why it is a supported mechanism rather than a hack:

  `sdk-bundle-Uqudo-3.10.0.aar` ships no `values-<lang>` folder of any kind — its `res/` has
  `values` and `values-night-v8` alongside the usual `drawable*`, `font`, `layout`, `navigation`,
  `raw` and screen-width `values-sw*dp-v13` buckets, but not one language bucket. So every string
  the customer sees on the SDK's scan and liveness screens falls back to English. R-002 recorded
  that correctly.

  R-002 also implied `setLocale('ar')` was inert, because the UI stayed English after S1-02 called
  it. That inference was wrong, and the bytecode says so: `UqudoSDK.setLocale` writes `key_locale`
  into the `uqudo_preferences` SharedPreferences, and the SDK's base Activity
  `io.uqudo.sdk.C.attachBaseContext` reads it back, builds a `Locale`, calls `LocaleList.setDefault`
  and `Configuration.setLocales`, then returns `createConfigurationContext(...)`. Every SDK activity
  has therefore been resolving its resources under locale `ar` all along. Only the Arabic values
  were missing. `PluginUqudoScanner`/`PluginUqudoFaceScanner` already call `setLocale('ar')` right
  after `init()` — and that order matters, because `init()` REMOVES `key_locale`.

  App-module resources win the AGP merge over a library's, so the keys below replace the AAR's under
  locale ar. Nothing is overlaid, subclassed or reflected into.

  *** THE WORDING IS PROVISIONAL. *** Drafted at S8-09, NOT yet through the product owner's
  native-Arabic review, and NOT yet seen on a device. BL-071 stays open for both. Entries whose
  layout is most likely to break — long copy on a 5-inch screen, embedded newlines, and bidi
  ordering where a placeholder or a digit sits inside an Arabic sentence — carry a RISK comment so
  the review and the device pass know where to look hardest.

  RELEASE-BUILD NOTE, measured not assumed: 129 of these 134 keys carry their Arabic into the
  release APK. The other five — `uq_confirm`, `uq_error_permission_denied`, `uq_error_retry`,
  `uq_error_forbidden`, `uq_error_payload_too_large` — are absent from the release resource table
  ENTIRELY, their English defaults included, because the release resource shrinker found nothing
  referencing them. So this is not an override failing to merge and it is not a language
  regression: there is no string of any language behind those five in a release build, and the
  code path that would have shown them was shrunk away with them. They are kept here because they
  are correct, cost nothing, and apply in a debug build or if the shrinker's analysis changes.
  If any of those five messages is ever seen in ENGLISH on a device, this analysis is wrong.

  Deliberately NOT overridden: `uq_api_base_url` and `uq_face_active_liveness` (both
  translatable="false" — they are configuration, not copy); the NFC/reading, lookup/OTP, background
  check and PDF-upload flows, none of which this journey enables; and the document descriptions of
  countries other than Sudan.
-->
<!--
  `tools:ignore="ExtraTranslation"` is load-bearing, not tidying. Every key below is defined only
  here, because its default lives in the Uqudo AAR rather than in this module's `values/strings.xml`
  — and lint does not count a library's defaults. `ExtraTranslation` is a FATAL lint issue, and
  `lintVitalRelease` sits in the release assembly graph, so without this the RELEASE build fails
  with 133 errors while the debug build passes happily. Reviewer-found at S8-09: the original proof
  was a debug build, which never runs `lintVital`. The pilot APK is a release build.

  The alternative — copying 133 English defaults into `values/strings.xml` — would fork the SDK's
  own copy into this repo and let it drift silently at the next SDK upgrade. Suppressing the check
  is the correct call here, not the lazy one.
-->
